+# cluster ci-f10986b0b93b91c1 — mingw64 build: ALSA-only test helpers left unguarded
+
+## Verdict
+
+REAL. The hosted `mingw64` job failed at `31f559ab479dcd1b822545aae477222f58f32c0d`
+while compiling `tests/src/core/MidiOutTimingTest.cpp`:
+
+```text
+tests/src/core/MidiOutTimingTest.cpp:107:6: error: 'void {anonymous}::measureAgainstRequested(...)' defined but not used [-Werror=unused-function]
+tests/src/core/MidiOutTimingTest.cpp:83:8: error: '{anonymous}::Jitter {anonymous}::measure(...)' defined but not used [-Werror=unused-function]
+cc1plus: all warnings being treated as errors
+```
+
+The translation unit defined `Jitter`, `measure` and `measureAgainstRequested` in the
+anonymous namespace outside any ALSA guard (`tests/src/core/MidiOutTimingTest.cpp:73-121`
+before the fix), but their only call sites are `run()` at
+`tests/src/core/MidiOutTimingTest.cpp:288-289`, inside the class section guarded by
+`#ifdef LMMS_HAVE_ALSA` (`:268`). MinGW64 has no ALSA, so all three definitions had
+internal linkage and no use, and the project's `-Werror` turned the warning into the
+hosted build failure. This is a test-target build-portability defect; product sources,
+save formats, commands and the realtime path are untouched.
+
+## Fix
+
+The existing `#ifdef LMMS_HAVE_ALSA` now starts before the first ALSA-only helper
+(`tests/src/core/MidiOutTimingTest.cpp:69`) and still closes at `:260`, so the constants,
+`Jitter`, `measure`, `measureAgainstRequested` and the receiver/loopback helpers all
+compile out together on a non-ALSA build. The ALSA header block (`:55`), the runtime
+ALSA-unavailable `QSKIP` (`:318`) and every assertion and test body are unchanged.
+
+A scan of the other ALSA-conditional test sources found only `MidiOutQueueTest.cpp`,
+`AudioDeviceDiagnosticsTest.cpp` and `CpuDiagnosticsDialogTest.cpp`; the hosted log shows
+those targets built successfully at the same commit, so no sibling has this defect.
+
+## Regression
+
+New mode `midi-out-timing-no-alsa` in `tests/train-41-portability-check.py:230`,
+registered as CTest `Train41-midi-out-timing-no-alsa` in `tests/CMakeLists.txt:9385`.
+It is deterministic and compile-only: it reuses the build's recorded
+`compile_commands.json` flags for the real translation unit, places a shadow
+`lmmsconfig.h` first on the include path (the generated header defines ALSA and has no
+include guard, so the shadow includes it and then `#undef LMMS_HAVE_ALSA`), regenerates
+the meta-object with `moc -ULMMS_HAVE_ALSA`, and compiles with
+`-Werror=unused-function`. There is no clock, sleep, thread or render in the check; the
+only input is the tree and the build database.
+
